<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agamemnon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agamemnon is the legendary king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mycenae">Mycenae</a> who, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iliad">Iliad</a>, led the Greek army against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a>. Son of Atreus and brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelaus">Menelaus</a>, he sacrificed his daughter Iphigenia for a fair wind and on his return was murdered by his wife Clytemnestra, a story dramatised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aeschylus">Aeschylus</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-schliemann">Heinrich Schliemann</a> named a gold funeral mask from Mycenae after him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agamemnon.jpg" alt="Agamemnon" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jastrow · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lekanis_Agamemnon_MNA_Taranto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
